note: Fitted on the fit window alone. Each step of the test is priced from its own inputs (request rate, prompt and output lengths, prompt-length spread, the replicas each role served), read over the same window its measurement covers, and never from its measured latency.
note: Each step is measured at its last cycle, over the rate window its histogram was read over (the router's, recorded with it; the engines' one minute): a step shorter than the window is measured over the window, so neighbouring steps share requests and are not independent. A step whose window reaches before the test, or over a change of replicas, is not judged. A percentile is scored with 50 requests or more at p50, 100 at p90 and 200 at p95 (50 for the mean); measured percentiles are interpolated inside the histogram's buckets.
note: Median ratio is the middle step's predicted over measured; typical and worst-10% miss the median and p90 of the factor between them; under the upper bound the share measured at or under the planner's own upper estimate, where it gives one; within, the share inside 20%. A measured figure above the histogram's top bucket counts as read low.
note: In region: the figure falls within the conditions our own accuracy benchmarks cover (docs/guides/capacity-planner/accuracy.md).
The planner's figures are a model, not a bound: this check measures how far off they are on this fleet.
